# ===========================================================================
# WAVE Q1 (2026-08-29) -- CONSOLIDATION OF THE results/validation ALLOW-LIST
# ===========================================================================
# THE INVARIANT THIS LIST EXISTS TO ENFORCE, stated once instead of being
# re-explained per wave above: `results/validation/*` is ignored because it is
# mostly regenerable output, and each artifact that is EVIDENCE -- something a
# reviewer must be able to read without a Docker run, or something a later wave
# compares against -- is re-included by name. The per-wave comments above give
# the reason for each; they are kept as written.
#
# WHAT WAS WRONG, and it is the failure mode the ignore rule was supposed to
# prevent in the first place: 38 artifacts were TRACKED but had NO negation
# rule. They are in git only because someone ran `git add -f` once. For those
# files `git status` stays silent when a regenerated copy differs or goes
# missing, `git check-ignore` reports them ignored, and the next person to
# delete-and-regenerate one has to know to force-add it again -- exactly the
# trap the Wave J1 comment at the top of this section describes. The list below
# closes that gap. It was derived mechanically (every path in
# `git ls-files results/validation/` that `git check-ignore --no-index` still
# matched), not by hand, so it is complete as of this commit.
#
# IF YOU ADD A TRACKED ARTIFACT UNDER results/validation/, ADD ITS NEGATION HERE.
# The check is one line:
#   git ls-files results/validation/ | while read f; do \
#       git check-ignore -q --no-index "$f" && echo "UNNEGATED: $f"; done
# It must print nothing.

# -- the cutover exam: the authoritative out-of-sample accuracy artifact, and
#    the one the README, the model card and three test files all read.
!results/validation/cutover_final_exam.json
!results/validation/cutover_final_exam.md
!results/validation/cutover_prereg.md
!results/validation/d1_exam_panel_reconciliation.json
!results/validation/d1_exam_panel_reconciliation.md

